// The S-expression dumper. This is how the reader is tested: golden-file
// comparison of these strings is the only cheap, exact check on a parser in a
// language with no reflection and no structured output.
//
// It is fully generic -- it never asks what kind a node is except to handle the
// four leaf shapes that are not "(name fields kids)". That is only possible
// because every kind stores node ids in a/b/c; see ast/kind/dcl/a.id.
//
// The result is built with string `+`, which is quadratic. That is acceptable
// here and nowhere else: a dump happens once, off the frame path.

ast_dump(int nd) {
  string ast_sexp_v = ast_sexp(nd);
  print(ast_sexp_v);
} return void;

ast_sexp(int nd) {
  int ast_kd_v = ast_kd(nd);
  string ret_s = ast_sexp_body(nd, ast_kd_v);
} return string ret_s;

// Written through a cell rather than returned, because the fall-through arm must
// not be evaluated when an earlier arm matches: ast_form on a `num` node would
// read ast_a as a node id and index the arena out of range, which aborts.
ast_sexp2(int nd, int kd, string[] strs) {
  if (kd = ast_k_num()) { string ast_numtx_v = ast_numtx(nd); sset(strs, 0, ast_numtx_v); }
  else if (kd = ast_k_ident()) { string ast_tx_v = ast_tx(nd); sset(strs, 0, ast_tx_v); }
  else { ast_sexp3(nd, kd, strs); }
} return void;
